+Two regressions to repair in dsa_python.py.
+
+REGRESSION 1 - the body of scale_new_list uses slice assignment, writing through a subscript on the left-hand side of the equals sign. That is in-place mutation and it is precisely the behaviour this function exists to contrast against, so the demo now proves the opposite of its lesson. The left-hand side of the assignment must be the bare parameter name with no subscript, no slice, and no brackets of any kind. Rebinding a plain name is the entire point. Verify by eye before you finish: if there is a square bracket anywhere to the left of that equals sign, it is still wrong.
+
+REGRESSION 2 - the main guard now calls only the Demo 1 functions. The calls for the other three demos were deleted, so increment_immutable, mutable_default_trap and shallow_aliasing are defined but never run. Restore calls to all three, after Demo 1, in that order, each under its own numbered comment matching the style already used for Demo 1. Demo 2 needs a local integer variable that is printed before and after the call so the reader sees it unchanged. The other two take no arguments and print their own output.
+
+Do not modify the four function definitions other than the single assignment line named in regression 1.

