+Create a generator script that reads the finished teaching script at /mnt/data/gitfiles/EPGP_Agentic_GenerativeAI/DSA/dsa_python.py and writes a Jupyter notebook to /mnt/data/gitfiles/EPGP_Agentic_GenerativeAI/DSA/dsa_python.ipynb. The notebook library is NOT installed, so build the notebook as an ordinary dictionary and serialise it with the standard library json module. Parse the source using the standard library abstract syntax tree module together with the helper that returns the exact source segment for a node; do not attempt to parse Python with regular expressions.
+
+Notebook envelope: nbformat four, nbformat_minor five, metadata declaring a python3 kernelspec named Python 3 and a language_info entry naming python. Every markdown cell needs the keys a notebook reader expects for its type, and every code cell additionally needs an execution count of null and an empty outputs list. Cell source may be given as a single string.
+
+The script must determine which section each top level function belongs to. Sections are delimited by the comment lines in the source whose text begins with the word SECTION after the hash character. Anything defined before the first such comment belongs to section one. Record each section comment's line number and its title text.
+
+Cells to emit, in source order:
+
+Start with one markdown cell holding a top level heading naming the study notes and the book, followed by the module docstring text of the source file.
+
+At each section boundary emit a markdown cell holding a second level heading with that section's title text.
+
+For every top level function definition emit a markdown cell followed by a code cell. The markdown cell holds a third level heading with the function name rendered as inline code, and beneath it the function's docstring text with its indentation stripped; if a function has no docstring the markdown cell holds only the heading. The code cell holds the function's exact source segment.
+
+For functions in section one only: after the function's own code cell emit nothing extra, because several of them require arguments.
+
+For functions in the later sections, which all take no parameters: append to that same code cell a blank line followed by a line invoking the function, so each cell is self contained and runnable on its own.
+
+After the last section one function, emit a markdown cell with a third level heading announcing the section one demonstrations, then a code cell containing the driver statements taken from the main guard at the bottom of the source. Take the guard's body, remove one level of indentation from every line, and keep only the leading portion up to but not including the first statement that calls a function whose name begins with the demo underscore prefix. Those later calls are redundant because the later sections already invoke themselves.
+
+Never emit the main guard itself as a cell.
+
+Print a summary line reporting how many markdown cells and how many code cells were written.

