# 2026-08-11 18:10:53.664010
+build_nb.py crashes with AttributeError because it defines its own get_source_segment helper that reads a made-up attribute named source_code off the syntax node. No such attribute exists on a node. Delete that hand-rolled helper entirely.
+
+The real function already exists in the standard library and its exact call form is: ast.get_source_segment(source, node) where source is the complete text of the file as one string and node is the syntax node. It returns the node's original source text, or None if position information is unavailable. Use it everywhere the deleted helper was called, and pass it the same full source string that was handed to ast.parse.
+
+Similarly, obtain a function's documentation text with the exact call ast.get_docstring(node), never by reaching into node internals.
+
+Change nothing else about the script's structure or its output format.

