# 2026-08-11 18:12:16.962890
+build_nb.py produces a structurally wrong notebook. It currently groups everything by section first, which destroys the document order: both section headings land at the very top, before any content. It also emits a separate cell that calls every single function, including ones that require arguments, so those cells would raise as soon as anyone ran them. Rewrite the cell emission using the single pass algorithm below and keep the notebook envelope, metadata and json serialisation exactly as they are.
+
+Build one combined list of events before emitting anything. Each event is a pair of a line number and a payload. There are two kinds. A heading event, one per raw source line whose stripped text opens with a hash followed by the word SECTION, carrying the title text after the hash. A function event, one per top level function definition in the parsed module, carrying the node. Sort this combined list by line number ascending. This ordering is the whole point: it interleaves headings and functions exactly as they appear in the file.
+
+Now emit the opening markdown cell with the top level heading and the module documentation text. Then walk the sorted event list once, in order, appending cells as you go.
+
+On a heading event append a single markdown cell containing a second level heading with the title.
+
+On a function event append exactly two cells and no more. First a markdown cell with a third level heading holding the function name in inline code backticks, followed by the function's documentation text with indentation stripped, omitting that text when there is none. Second, one code cell holding the function's original source. Whether that code cell also ends with a call to the function is decided by one rule and one rule only: append a blank line and an invocation line if and only if the function's parameter list is empty. Functions that declare parameters get no invocation. The invocation belongs inside this same code cell; never emit a standalone cell whose only content is a call.
+
+After the walk finishes, append the closing markdown cell announcing the demonstrations for the functions that take arguments, and then the driver code cell, both exactly as already specified, built from the dedented leading portion of the main guard body up to the first call to a demo prefixed function.
+
+Sanity check to print at the end alongside the existing counts: the number of code cells must equal the number of function definitions plus one.

