+
+Mistake one, variable shadowing. It assigned the result of extracting one function's source back onto the very variable holding the entire file's text. Every later extraction then received a fragment instead of the file and eventually crashed. The variable holding the full file text is read only for the whole run. Give the per function extraction its own distinct name.
+
+Mistake two, recursive tree traversal. It collected function definitions by walking the tree recursively, which descends into function bodies and class bodies and therefore captured inner helper functions and special methods that are implementation details of a demo. Only definitions sitting at the outermost level of the module are wanted. Iterate the module node's own body list directly and select the function definitions from it. Do not use the recursive walker anywhere.
+
+Mistake three, a broken notion of sections. It stored sections in a dictionary keyed by title while a single running variable tracked the current one, so every function was filed under whichever section happened to be found last. Sections are not needed as groupings at all. Do not build any section to function mapping.
+
+THE ALGORITHM.
+
+Read the file text once. Parse it once.
+
+Collect heading events by scanning the numbered raw lines for those whose stripped text opens with a hash then the word SECTION; the payload is the text following the hash.
+
+Collect function events from the module body's top level function definitions only; the payload is the node.
+
+Merge both kinds into one list of line number and payload pairs and sort ascending by line number.
+
+Emit the opening markdown cell: a top level heading naming these as study notes for the Goodrich book, then the module's documentation text.
+
+Walk the sorted list once. A heading event yields one markdown cell with a second level heading. A function event yields exactly two cells: a markdown cell with a third level heading containing the function name inside backticks plus its documentation text when present, then one code cell whose content is that function's extracted source, and to which a blank line and a call to the function are appended only when the function declares no parameters at all.
+
+Then locate the main guard, which is the sole top level conditional statement at the end of the module. Determine the line number of the first statement inside it that is a bare call to a function whose name begins with the demo underscore prefix. Take the raw file lines from just after the guard's own line up to but excluding that line, strip exactly four leading spaces from each, and emit a markdown cell with a third level heading announcing the argument taking demonstrations followed by a code cell holding those lines.
+
+Finally print how many markdown and how many code cells were produced. Do not assert anything.

