# 2026-08-11 18:16:46.130542
+Throw away everything in build_nb.py and write a new, much simpler version. Keep only the notebook envelope, its metadata, and the json serialisation.
+
+The previous attempts all failed because they parsed the source into a syntax tree. Do not do that. Do not import the ast module at all. This input file is uniformly formatted and can be split reliably by looking at indentation alone, which is far simpler and also solves the nested function problem for free, because anything nested is indented and therefore never starts a block.
+
+Input file: /mnt/data/gitfiles/EPGP_Agentic_GenerativeAI/DSA/dsa_python.py
+Output file: /mnt/data/gitfiles/EPGP_Agentic_GenerativeAI/DSA/dsa_python.ipynb
+
+Step one, split into top level blocks. Read all lines. A new block begins at any non blank line that has zero leading whitespace. Every following line, blank or indented, belongs to that block until the next such line. Trim trailing blank lines from each finished block.
+
+Step two, classify each block by looking at its first line. A block whose first line starts with three double quote characters is the module documentation. A block whose first line, once stripped, starts with a hash followed by the word SECTION is a section heading, and its title is the text after the hash. A block whose first line starts with the keyword def is a function. A block whose first line starts with the characters that open the main guard conditional is the guard. Ignore any block matching none of these.
+
+Step three, emit cells in the order the blocks appeared, which is already correct because you never reorder anything.
+
+The module documentation block yields the opening markdown cell: a top level heading naming these as study notes for the Goodrich book, then that documentation text with its surrounding triple quotes removed.
+
+A section heading block yields one markdown cell with a second level heading holding the title.
+
+A function block yields two cells. First a markdown cell with a third level heading holding the function name inside backticks; the name is the text between the def keyword and the opening parenthesis. If the block's body opens with a triple quoted documentation string, include its text underneath the heading, with the quotes removed and the indentation stripped. Second a code cell holding the block text exactly as it appeared. Append to that code cell a blank line and a line calling the function, but only when the text between the first opening parenthesis and its closing parenthesis on the def line contains nothing but whitespace.
+
+The guard block yields a markdown cell with a third level heading announcing the demonstrations that need arguments, then a code cell. Build that cell from the guard's body lines, that is every line after its first. Remove exactly four leading spaces from each. Stop before the first line whose stripped text begins with the demo underscore prefix, discarding it and everything after.
+
+Finally print the counts of markdown and code cells.

