# 2026-08-11 19:32:41.357357
+Create a bash wrapper script that runs aider against a local Ollama model, so that the caller can never forget the safety steps that were repeatedly missed by hand.
+
+It takes a message string and one or more file paths. Provide a switch that selects between two modes. The default mode targets edits to files that already exist and must use the seven billion parameter coder model at the q3_K_M quantisation with aider's diff edit format. The alternate mode, selected by a new-file switch, targets creating files from nothing and must use the three billion parameter coder model at q8_0 with aider's whole edit format. Never pair the three billion model with the diff format; that combination hangs indefinitely and must be impossible to select through this script.
+
+Both modes always pass aider the flags that skip confirmation prompts, disable aider's own git handling, disable URL detection, and disable the repository map by setting its token budget to zero.
+
+The aider binary lives at /mnt/data/gitfiles/.venv/bin/aider. The Ollama endpoint is chosen at runtime: probe the local one on the loopback address at the standard Ollama port with a two second limit, and if that does not answer, fall back to the host at 100.123.203.85 on the same port. Export that choice in the variable aider reads for the Ollama base URL.
+
+Wrap the aider invocation in a hard time limit, defaulting to ten minutes, overridable by an environment variable so a caller can shorten or extend it. Aider must run in the foreground; never background it.
+
+The critical part: install an exit trap, before aider starts, that always runs on the way out whether aider succeeded, failed, or was interrupted. That trap must ask the Ollama server which models are currently loaded and issue a stop for each one, then report the remaining GPU memory in use. This is the step whose absence left orphaned model runners holding video memory.
+
+Print, before running, which model and edit format were chosen and which endpoint is in use. Exit with aider's own status code. If no message or no files are supplied, print a short usage line and exit non zero.

