# 2026-08-11 19:41:41.823966
+Write a bash wrapper that invokes aider against a local Ollama model and makes the safety steps impossible to forget.
+
+Usage: a required message string via a -m switch, an optional --new switch, then one or more file paths.
+
+Mode selection. Without --new it edits existing files: use model ollama/qwen2.5-coder:7b-instruct-q3_K_M with aider's diff edit format. With --new it creates files: use ollama/qwen2.5-coder:3b-instruct-q8_0 with aider's whole edit format. The three billion model must never be paired with diff; that hangs forever, so make the pairing unreachable.
+
+Always pass aider: --yes-always, --no-git, --no-detect-urls, --map-tokens 0. Binary path is /mnt/data/gitfiles/.venv/bin/aider.
+
+Endpoint: probe http://localhost:11434 with a two second curl limit; if it fails use http://100.123.203.85:11434. Export the result as OLLAMA_API_BASE.
+
+Logging, important. Send aider's combined output through tee into a timestamped log file under a logs directory beside this script, while still showing it on the terminal. Pipe stdbuf with line buffering ahead of aider so output appears as it is produced rather than in blocks. A killed run must still leave a readable partial log; do not let a trailing pager or tail swallow the stream.
+
+Time limit: wrap aider in timeout, defaulting to 600 seconds, overridable through an environment variable.
+
+Cleanup trap, the critical part. Install it before aider starts so it fires on success, failure and interruption alike. It must query the Ollama server for loaded models, issue a stop for each, and then print current GPU memory usage. Absence of this step is what left orphaned runners holding video memory.
+
+Before running, echo the chosen model, edit format, endpoint and log path. Exit with aider's own exit status. With no message or no files, print one usage line and exit non-zero.

