# 2026-08-11 19:42:36.854831
+Four defects in aider-local. Fix all four, change nothing else.
+
+DEFECT ONE, invalid flags. The edit format variable holds --diff or --whole. Neither is a real aider option. Aider selects the format with the two-token option --edit-format followed by the bare word diff or the bare word whole. Store only the bare word in the variable and supply the option name at the call site.
+
+DEFECT TWO, malformed invocation. The final command passes the model, the message and the edit format as bare positional words, so aider receives them as filenames. The model must be introduced by --model, the message by --message, and the format as described above. Only the file paths are positional, and they must come last.
+
+DEFECT THREE, the cleanup trap is an unimplemented stub containing a placeholder comment and an example that does nothing. This trap is the entire reason the script exists. Implement it for real: ask the Ollama server which models are currently loaded by requesting its process endpoint, which is the path /api/ps on the exported base URL and which replies with JSON holding a models array whose entries each carry a name field; for every name found, run the ollama stop command against it. Then print the GPU memory currently in use, querying only the used and total memory fields rather than dumping the full nvidia-smi table. Guard the whole trap so that a missing server or missing nvidia-smi cannot make it fail.
+
+DEFECT FOUR, the log path is relative to whatever directory the caller happens to be in, and its parent is never created. Anchor it to a logs directory sitting beside the script itself, resolved from the script's own location rather than the working directory, and create that directory if absent before logging starts.

