# 2026-08-11 19:44:49.411690
+Two remaining defects in aider-local. Fix only these.
+
+DEFECT ONE, the trap stops nothing. It sends a POST to a URL formed by joining the base address, the word stop, and the model name. There is no such route on an Ollama server and it answers 404, so no model is ever unloaded and the orphaned runner problem this script exists to solve remains. Unloading is done through the command line client, not the HTTP API: the exact invocation is 'ollama stop NAME' where NAME is the model name. Keep reading the currently loaded names from the process endpoint with jq as it already does, but drive that command for each name instead of curl. Also rename the loop variable, because it currently reuses the name of the variable holding the chosen model and clobbers it.
+
+DEFECT TWO, logging dies immediately on a clean machine. The log path points at a logs directory beside the script, but nothing ever creates that directory, so the redirection through tee fails on first use. Create the directory, including any missing parents, before the redirection is established. Order matters: the creation must happen earlier in the script than the line that sets up the tee redirection.

