# 2026-08-11 19:45:31.205639
+One wrong binary in the cleanup function of aider-local. Inside the loop that unloads each currently loaded model, the command being run is the aider executable from the virtual environment. Aider has no stop subcommand and cannot unload anything; this silently does nothing. Unloading models is the job of the Ollama command line client, which on this machine lives at /usr/local/bin/ollama. Invoke that binary with its stop subcommand and the model name. Change only that one command inside the loop; leave the surrounding function, the trap registration and the rest of the script exactly as they are.

