+
+The first row currently sends any file edit or creation to the three billion model using the whole edit format, with a parenthetical saying diff is unreliable for it. Measurements on 2026-08-11 supersede this. Split that single row into two, because creating a file and editing an existing one now route differently.
+
+New first row: editing a file that already exists. Model is the seven billion coder at q3_K_M. Method is aider with the diff edit format and the repository map disabled by giving its token budget a value of zero. Note that this was measured at twenty five seconds and three hundred fifty eight output tokens for a surgical single line change in a file of three hundred ninety five lines, and that unlike the whole format it structurally cannot delete code it was not asked to touch.
+
+New second row: creating a brand new file from nothing. Model is the three billion coder at q8_0. Method is aider with the whole edit format. Note that whole format is acceptable here only because a new file starts empty, and that it becomes unsafe once a file exceeds roughly one hundred and fifty lines.
+
+Add a further row recording a forbidden combination: the three billion model with the diff edit format. Method column states that this must never be used because it hangs, having been observed to run four hundred seconds against a three hundred ninety five line file while producing no edit at all.
+
+Leave the existing rows about conflict markers, quick questions, explaining code and architecture exactly as they are, apart from the row for hard subtle tasks, whose note should now say the seven billion model is fully GPU resident at one hundred percent with flash attention and q8_0 key value cache enabled.

