# 2026-08-11 19:50:28.334052
+Append a new section to the very end of CLAUDE.md, after the existing benchmarked findings. Do not modify anything already in the file.
+
+Title it as benchmarked findings for the RTX 2060 dated 2026-08-11, and note it supplements rather than replaces the earlier June findings. Write it as a short list of bullet points, each stating a finding and the evidence for it, in the same terse style as the existing findings section.
+
+Cover these seven points.
+
+Flash attention combined with an eight bit key value cache is now enabled in the Ollama systemd unit. It cut the seven billion q3_K_M model's footprint at ten thousand context from 4.91 GB down to 4.46 GB, moving it from ninety one percent resident with 447 MB spilling to fully resident with all twenty nine layers on the GPU. Quality cost is negligible.
+
+The service also now limits itself to one loaded model at a time and unloads thirty seconds after idle. Before this, the default allowed several models resident simultaneously with a five minute idle window.
+
+Killing the aider client does not stop the Ollama runner. The server keeps generating and keeps the model loaded, so every interrupted run used to strand video memory. Two stranded runners once held 5.4 GB, which made a benchmark offload a single layer and report a meaningless 7.4 tokens per second. This is why the one model limit and short idle window matter.
+
+The diff edit format on the seven billion model is now the default for editing existing files, replacing whole format. Evidence: a single line change inside a 395 line file took 25s and 358 output tokens and altered nothing else, whereas whole format repeatedly dropped entire unrelated functions because it must regenerate every line of the file each time.
+
+The diff format must never be paired with the three billion model. It ran 400s against the same file and produced no edit.
+
+The model tagged qwen3.5:4b looks attractive at a 3.4 GB download but is a trap on this card. Its long context architecture inflates the real footprint to 6.51 GB, leaving it seventy two percent resident at 27.7 tokens per second, roughly half the speed of the seven billion q3 model, and it failed to return anything through aider within ten minutes. Judge a model by its loaded footprint, never its download size.
+
+A prompting rule that repeatedly worked: when a small model keeps producing the same wrong structure, restating the goal does not help. Name the specific construct it keeps reaching for and forbid it outright. Telling the model that a loop keyword must not appear and that it should instead write six statements in sequence fixed on the first attempt what four goal restatements had failed to fix.
+
+Also add a final bullet on invocation hygiene: always route aider output through tee into a log file rather than a trailing pager, because a pager buffers and a killed run then leaves no diagnostic at all; and always give aider an explicit time limit.

